---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';
import { u } from '../../utils/site';

const ghAction = [
  { kind: 'cmd' as const, text: '- uses: nitishagar/lumen/action@v0.4.0' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '  with:' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '    url: https://example.com' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '    fail-threshold: warning' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '    baseline: lumen.baseline.json   # gate only on NEW findings' },
];
const gitlab = [
  { kind: 'cmd' as const, text: 'audit:' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '  script:' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '    - npx -y @lumen-seo/cli@0 audit "$SITE_URL" --format sarif --out lumen.sarif' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '  artifacts:' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '    paths: [lumen.sarif]' },
];
const shell = [
  { kind: 'cmd' as const, text: 'npx -y @lumen-seo/cli@0 audit https://example.com \\' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: '  --format sarif --out lumen.sarif --fail-threshold warning' },
  { kind: 'out' as const, text: 'echo "exit $?  # 0 ok · 1 findings at/above threshold · 2 config error"' },
];
const summary = [
  { kind: 'cmd' as const, text: 'npx @lumen-seo/cli audit "$SITE_URL" --format md >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"' },
];
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Lumen in CI"
  description="Wire lumen into GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or any shell: SARIF for code scanning, a Markdown job summary, and baseline-gated regressions."
  activeHref="/docs/ci/"
  toc={[
    { id: 'github', label: 'GitHub Actions' },
    { id: 'monitoring', label: 'Monitoring recipe' },
    { id: 'sarif', label: 'SARIF' },
    { id: 'summary', label: 'Job summary' },
    { id: 'baseline', label: 'Baseline gate' },
    { id: 'gitlab', label: 'GitLab CI' },
    { id: 'shell', label: 'Any shell' },
    { id: 'exit', label: 'Exit codes' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    lumen is built for CI: one command, one exit-code contract, and two CI-native
    render formats — <code>--format sarif</code> (2.1.0, validated against the
    official schema) and <code>--format md</code> (a job summary). Previews on
    localhost work with <code>--allow-private</code> (the Action infers it for
    loopback URLs automatically).
  </p>

  <h2 id="github">GitHub Actions</h2>
  <p>
    The composite action under <code>nitishagar/lumen/action</code> starts an
    optional preview server, audits it, uploads the SARIF artifact, and writes
    the Markdown summary to <code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>:
  </p>
  <Code lines={ghAction} />
  <p>
    To surface findings as PR annotations, upload the artifact to code scanning
    with <code>github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3</code> — see the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/nitishagar/lumen/tree/main/action">action README</a>{' '}
    for the full snippet and the pinning note.
  </p>

  <h2 id="monitoring">Scheduled monitoring (recipe)</h2>
  <p>
    lumen has no daemon — the recipe is a cron workflow that commits audit
    history to a dedicated branch. It's yours to own (copy, adjust the
    schedule, pin the version):
  </p>
  <Code lines={[
    { kind: 'out', text: '# .github/workflows/lumen-monitor.yml (your repo)' },
    { kind: 'out', text: 'on:' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '  schedule: [{ cron: "0 6 * * 1" }]  # weekly' },
    { kind: 'out', text: 'permissions: { contents: write }' },
    { kind: 'out', text: 'jobs:' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '  audit:' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '    runs-on: ubuntu-latest' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '    steps:' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '      - uses: actions/checkout@<pinned-sha>' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '      - run: npx -y @lumen-seo/cli@0 audit https://example.com \\' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          --max-pages 100 --fail-threshold off \\' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          && npx -y @lumen-seo/cli@0 history audit --json > trend.json' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '      - run: |' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          git config user.name lumen-monitor && git config user.email bot@users.noreply.github.com' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          git checkout -B lumen-history' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          git add trend.json && git commit -m "audit $(date -u +%F)" || true' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '          git push origin lumen-history' },
  ]} />
  <p>
    Trend lines come from <code>lumen history audit</code> — and the branch
    history doubles as a shareable record. (<code>--fail-threshold off</code>{' '}
    keeps monitoring non-gating; drop it if you want the cron to alarm.)
  </p>

  <h2 id="sarif">SARIF</h2>
  <p>
    <code>--format sarif</code> emits one rule per lumen rule (with its{' '}
    <a href={u('/docs/rules-reference/')}>rules-reference anchor</a> as{' '}
    <code>helpUri</code>), one result per finding, and the run's provenance
    (version, budgets, started/completed, incomplete/stopReason) in{' '}
    <code>run.properties</code>. With <code>--out</code>, the artifact is
    written and stdout stays silent; without it, the document goes to stdout.
  </p>
  <Code lines={[
    { kind: 'cmd', text: 'npx @lumen-seo/cli audit https://example.com --format sarif --out lumen.sarif' },
  ]} />
  <p>
    <code>--source-map site/src/pages/**</code> adds a best-effort page-URL →
    source-file mapping for annotations; when the mapping is ambiguous the
    result stays URL-only — never guessed. The audit seed's own subpath is
    stripped first, so previews served under a base (Astro{' '}
    <code>base: '/lumen'</code>) map to the same files; GitHub code scanning
    rejects <code>http</code> locations, so a source map is required for
    annotation uploads.
  </p>

  <h2 id="summary">Job summary</h2>
  <Code lines={summary} />
  <p>
    The summary carries the score, the top rule groups with fixes (linking the
    rules reference), and — when baselined — the new/fixed/unknown breakdown.
  </p>

  <h2 id="baseline">Baseline gate</h2>
  <p>
    Adopt lumen on a site with existing findings: record a baseline once, commit
    it, and gate only on regressions in CI:
  </p>
  <Code lines={[
    { kind: 'cmd', text: 'npx @lumen-seo/cli audit "$SITE_URL" --update-baseline lumen.baseline.json' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '# commit lumen.baseline.json, then in CI:' },
    { kind: 'cmd', text: 'npx @lumen-seo/cli audit "$SITE_URL" --baseline lumen.baseline.json' },
    { kind: 'out', text: '# exit 1 only when NEW findings appear at/above failThreshold' },
  ]} />
  <p>
    Fingerprints are <code>rule + normalized URL + selector</code> — message
    tweaks never un-baseline an issue; pages not audited in a run are{' '}
    <em>unknown</em>, never counted as fixed. Compare any two saved reports
    with <code>lumen diff a.json b.json</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="gitlab">GitLab CI</h2>
  <Code lines={gitlab} />

  <h2 id="shell">Any shell</h2>
  <Code lines={shell} />

  <h2 id="exit">Exit codes</h2>
  <p>
    The contract is stable across every renderer: <code>0</code> under
    threshold, <code>1</code> findings at/above <code>failThreshold</code> (or
    new findings with <code>--baseline</code>; an incomplete run always gates),
    <code>2</code> usage/config error.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
